<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon, adaptive form (API 26+).

  This file not existing was the whole bug. Without it a launcher has nothing to
  build an icon from, so it falls back to the legacy mipmap-*/ic_launcher.png — a
  full-bleed square bitmap with no notion of a mask — and crops that square to its
  own shape. On a launcher that uses circles, that is exactly "a blocky square
  image inside the circle".

  The layers are a flat brand background and the mark; a launcher supplies the
  shape. The monochrome layer is for Android 13+ themed icons, which tint it with
  the system palette using the alpha channel only, so it needs no artwork of its
  own — the same vector serves.

  ic_launcher_round.xml is deliberately identical: roundIcon exists for launchers
  that want a rounder shape, and the adaptive format is already shape-agnostic.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
